//! What `substConstants` does with each kind of new value, by where sigmastate looks at it:
//! `Platform.liftToConstant` lifts every item of the new values by its runtime class and the
//! version of the tree being evaluated (v6.0.6 `data/jvm/.../sigma/Platform.scala:16-63`), a
//! collection whole, and the constant writer reads a lifted value only where its position is
//! written.
//!
//! GENERATED from the measured rows of queue item 28's round (`gen_rows_test.py`); do not edit
//! by hand. Every outcome, value and cost is that of the sigma-state 6.0.7 jars. Their context
//! had one header, a pre-header whose parent it is, a P2PK self box and no context variable;
//! [`context`] sets those, which is everything a row reads. The `source` rows have a context
//! of their own, [`source_context`].
//!
//! A row's name is `<where>|<kind>|<position>|v<tree version>`.
//!
//! Where: `item` (an item of the new values), `in-coll` and `in-coll2` (inside a collection
//! that is an item, one and two deep), `tuple-const` (the middle item of a tuple constant that
//! is the new values), `tuple-const-items` and `if-tuple-const-items` (a tuple constant of
//! three `Int`s as the new values, bare and behind an `If`), `own-empty` (written over an empty
//! collection constant of its own type), `new-values` (a `Coll[String]` constant, a pair),
//! `no-items`, `twice` (two positions naming one constant), `template` (the template varies: a
//! constant of a tree version 3 type in it, the size bit), `string` (a `String` written over a
//! `String` constant, and not), `source` (a `Coll[String]` from a context variable and from a
//! register).
//!
//! Position: `pos7` and `pos789` (no constant there), `nocon` (a template without constants),
//! `other` (a constant of another type), `own` (a constant of its own type), `one-item`,
//! `no-item` and `template-alone` (of `own-empty`), `tree-template` (of `no-items`),
//! `int-written` and `nothing` (of `template`), `written-…` and `none-written` (of `string` and
//! `source`).
//!
//! The `CHANGED` tables hold the rows fork `a9297617` answered otherwise.

